      "observation": "The 30-yr fixed rate at 6.65% is a meaningful affordability headwind on a $1.6M+ asset class. At this rate, a conventional 80% LTV mortgage on a $1.7M purchase implies ~$9,100/month in principal and interest alone — well above the HUD FMR 2BR benchmark of $2,910/month, compressing investor yield support and limiting the pool of leveraged buyers.",
